// Built with docs/PROFILE_PLAYBOOK.md §9 (EV-RES-DATA, Nov 2 2026; build log docs/profiles/NVDA.md).
// NVIDIA's fiscal year ends in late January: 1Q27 = quarter to Apr 26 2026; annual 2027 = FY2027.
//
// Compares REPORTED actuals against three references, per period:
//   act     — GAAP lines from SEC EDGAR XBRL (10-K / 10-Q; fourth quarters = year − nine months); market platforms and
//             reportable-segment revenue from each quarter's CFO commentary (8-K Ex. 99.2, 4Q FY19 → 2Q FY27, pulled
//             2026-11-02); non-GAAP lines, EPS, capex, FCF and segment operating income from Bloomberg's reported
//             columns (BBG_CONSENSUS.txt; the newest file wins), tied to the releases. NVIDIA's non-GAAP stopped
//             excluding stock-based compensation in FY2027 (history restated): before 1Q27 every non-GAAP line is
//             the old figure adjusted by the SBC Bloomberg reports for that quarter, which reproduces NVIDIA's
//             restated 1Q26 / 2Q26. Hyperscale / ACIE after the 2Q FY27 reclassification (see their notes).
//   summit  — Summit DCF model (SAB), FROZEN on purpose, not live (playbook rule 10) — refresh by re-pulling when a
//             new snapshot is submitted. Three snapshots, pulled 2026-11-02: 2025-12-12 (after 3Q FY26) -> 4Q26 and
//             FY2026; 2026-03-04 (after 4Q FY26) -> 1Q27-2Q27; 2026-08-28 (after 2Q FY27) -> 3Q27-4Q27 and FY2027-FY2029.
//             BASIS: the 2025-12-12 file's adjusted lines exclude SBC (NVIDIA's old non-GAAP), so its non-GAAP op.
//             income, gross profit, model EBITDA and EPS are left out (null); its GAAP and revenue lines are used.
//             The Summit half of estMatrix and the `evolution` block come from the same dumps
//             (scripts/consensus/dumps/nvda_summit, map_summit_nvda.json). Labels: js/summit-map/nvda.js.
//   cons    — Bloomberg consensus (BBG_CONSENSUS.txt + Consensus_Portal.xlsm): the estMatrix block below, generated
//             by scripts/consensus/emit_matrix.py with map_nvda.json and spliced by apply_matrix.py; the flat arrays
//             carry the engine's pre-print pick for each period. Adjusted lines only from 2026-03-02 (first file
//             after NVIDIA's definition change); Hyperscale / ACIE only from 2026-09-09.
//   guideLo / guideHi — NVIDIA's outlook in the prior quarter's release: revenue (midpoint ± 2%) every quarter;
//             non-GAAP opex (single number) from 1Q27. Gross-margin guides are quoted in the notes, not drawn.
//
// All monetary values in US$ millions; EPS in dollars. null = not available.
// Arrays are parallel to `periods`. A period with act:null is an upcoming print.

